WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.288
Let’s walk through Build proposals.

00:00:02.288 --> 00:00:04.800
Build the proposal around a named recipient and a clear

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.888
exchange.

00:00:05.888 --> 00:00:08.950
Preserve what is offered, what is requested, timing

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.562
, conditions, and rationale so White Cell and each

00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:14.688
recipient can understand the same durable record.

00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:17.738
On this slide, use the Strategic Orientation and move

00:00:17.738 --> 00:00:20.212
tabs to see exactly what was noted for each part

00:00:20.212 --> 00:00:21.663
of the simulation.

00:00:21.663 --> 00:00:24.363
Create and revise your team's proposals here.

00:00:24.363 --> 00:00:27.363
Once submitted, they become read-only while White

00:00:27.363 --> 00:00:28.788
Cell reviews them.

00:00:29.335 --> 00:00:32.160
In practice, translate the room’s choice into a complete

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.485
proposal with enough evidence for the next reviewer to act

00:00:35.485 --> 00:00:35.623
.

00:00:35.623 --> 00:00:38.472
Before you continue, verify these points:

00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:42.148
Strategic Orientation establishes the opening position.

00:00:42.148 --> 00:00:45.648
Move tabs keep proposals attached to the correct round.

00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:49.935
Submitted or forwarded records become read-only at the documented boundary

00:00:49.935 --> 00:00:50.035
.

00:00:50.035 --> 00:00:52.810
When you are ready, use Open proposals to move

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.373
to the live surface.

00:00:54.373 --> 00:00:57.135
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:57.135 --> 00:00:57.285
.
